# Deploy Script Conventions

- Every script starts with `set -euo pipefail`.
- Resolve paths relative to the script's own location:
  `SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"` — never
  assume a working directory.
- `NAMESPACE` is always overridable via an env var with a default
  (`NAMESPACE="${NAMESPACE:-doc-gen-demo}"`).
- Idempotent by construction: use `oc apply`, `oc create ... --dry-run=client -o yaml | oc apply -f -`
  for ConfigMaps/Secrets, and check-before-create
  (`oc get X >/dev/null 2>&1 || oc create X`) for one-time setup steps
  like `oc new-build`.
- Echo a one-line `==>` status message before each major step so the
  script's output reads as a narrated log, matching the existing scripts.
- End with an explicit `oc rollout status` wait and print the resulting
  Route URL (if any) — don't leave the user guessing whether it worked.
- After editing any script, validate with `bash -n <script>` before
  committing.
